	(text "C128 USB-C PD Power Adapter v0.1 (DC only, no 50/60 Hz: the CIA TOD clocks will not tick from mains)\nNeeds a USB-C PD charger offering 15 V (>= 3 A / 45 W recommended). U1 (CH224A) requests 15 V via R1 = 56k.\nQ1 connects the 15 V rail only after the PD contract (PG low). U2 and U3 start only above ~13.3 V (EN UVLO).\nDIN (square 5-pin): 1 = +5.0 V / ~3 A (U2 SY8205 -> U4 eFuse: OVLO 5.64 V, 4.45 A limit; D1 TVS), 3 = +12.3 V DC (U3, D2 TVS) into the C128 \"9 VAC\" bridge,\n2 = GND, 4 = GND/NC, 5 = other 9 VAC leg tied to GND (pin numbers per the Drunk'n'Retro diagram).\nVERIFY THE SOCKET PINOUT ON YOUR C128 WITH A METER BEFORE FIRST POWER-UP."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
